entory) are computed from the schema + registries.'","src/rebar/_deprecations.py:91 `_permanent(\"cfg\", \"verify.overlap_enabled\", ...)` and :247-262 `_tomb(\"cfg\", ...)` are the authoritative per-key cfg lifecycle source.","gen_env_registry.py:132-145 already reads `rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY` for the env channel because the schema cannot supply alias/removal status — the cfg channel is the analogous need here.","src/rebar/_config_schema.py:44-54 the schema is a stdlib dataclass of keys/defaults, with no lifecycle field."],"finding":"The plan claims a per-key 'lifecycle' column is derivable from 'the config schema plus the ownership and secret-name registries', but the config schema (src/rebar/_config_schema.py) is a typed dataclass of keys/defaults/validation and carries no deprecation/removal lifecycle. Per-key config lifecycle lives in rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY (kind=='cfg', e.g. verify.overlap_enabled) and the tombstone registry (_tomb('cfg', ...) e.g. reconciler.lock_backend, code_health.analyzers) — the same registry gen_env_registry.py already reads for the env channel. The enumerated source list omits it, leaving the lifecycle column's data flow incomplete.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fad789ece0c810901","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Outcome / Plan step 1 / AC line 1 ('generates ... from the config schema plus the ownership and secret-name registries')","norm_id":"n4ca34501419d42a6","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A deprecated or tombstoned config key (e.g. reconciler.lock_backend) must appear in the lifecycle column but is invisible to a generator that only reads the schema dataclass.","The topic-coverage test asserts a 'lifecycle' anchor but the generator has no data to populate meaningful per-key lifecycle rows."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Extend the plan's source list to 'config schema + ownership registry + secret-name registry + rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY/tombstone registry (cfg kind)', and specify that the lifecycle column is derived from the cfg-kind deprecation and tombstone entries.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify per-doc topic ownership: define REQUIRED_TOPICS as a mapping (topic -> owning doc) or two lists, so the coverage test asserts each topic's anchor in its OWNING doc rather than every topic in both docs.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","E1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1875,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a test asserts docs/config-reference.md and docs/security.md each contain a heading/anchor for every entry in an explicit REQUIRED_TOPICS list'","AC: 'docs/config-reference.md and docs/security.md contain an anchor for every topic in the REQUIRED_TOPICS list'","Topics named mix config-reference concerns (observability exception, subprocess limitations, behavior deltas) with security concerns (restart/redeploy rotation, MCP/CLI exposure)"],"finding":"The topic-coverage test/AC says config-reference.md and security.md 'each contain a heading/anchor for every entry in REQUIRED_TOPICS', but the enumerated topics are split by concern (observability exception / subprocess limitations belong to the config reference; secret-name inventory / restart-redeploy rotation belong to security). Requiring EVERY topic in EACH doc conflicts with the split ownership; requiring only the union is unstated. The per-doc topic ownership is ambiguous.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8429362f569bbf74","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing (Topic coverage) and AC line 3","norm_id":"n03fae359a8b4d33e","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor writes both docs to contain all topics, producing redundant/incoherent security doc, or the test false-fails because security.md legitimately omits subprocess-limitations."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Replace the single REQUIRED_TOPICS-in-both assertion with a `{topic: doc}` map and assert each topic's anchor appears in its designated doc (union coverage across the two docs).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["4 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that REQUIRED_TOPICS is a hand-maintained list independent of the generator's own output/template, so the topic-coverage test can actually fail when a topic is dropped (not a self-referential tautology).","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a test asserts ... each contain a heading/anchor for every entry in an explicit REQUIRED_TOPICS list'","REQUIRED_TOPICS enumerates precisely the topics the generator is designed to emit; if it is generated from the same source as the doc, the test tautologically passes"],"finding":"The topic-coverage test asserts each generated doc contains an anchor for 'every entry in an explicit REQUIRED_TOPICS list'. If REQUIRED_TOPICS is derived from the same schema/registry/template that the generator emits, the assertion is a tautology (self-authored oracle) that passes by construction and cannot detect a genuinely missing topic